    "turn_text": "right, good morning. It is Monday, February 7th. Welcome to the show. Hope you had a fantastic weekend. Mine was all right. I got out of town a little bit for the weekend. Went to go do some birthday celebrating. Unfortunately, the birthday person couldn't make it to the party, which is okay. We just turned it around and made it about me. What? I know that it's not as bad as you think. Because my birthday's coming up, so we figured A. One birthday person's not gonna show up. We'll use the other one, right? Anyhow, I hope you did have a great weekend. This weekend, I experienced one of these things. I'll tell you about this story in a second, but we also have a coming up this morning. We do have Congressman Neil Dunn is going to be joining us in studio. We're going to have him once again for an entire hour. So we've got all kinds of questions to ask the Congressman. Plus, I want to get your questions as well. And you know that we always like to get these as rapid fires we possibly can. So I would love for you to send me. all the questions that Go there and there's a contact thing. Just click on contact and bam, you can send me a message that way as well so that I can ask the congressman these questions. When he comes on the show later on this morning, like I said, we have a congressman done for an entire hour and it's a big week this week too. We also have Marco Rubio is going to be on the show later this week. So that'll be another great interview. Lots to talk about with him, especially after what happened over the weekend. when he discussed at a, what was it that he was at? It was like a rally or a meeting or something or other, where he kind of, not fully, but he kind of went right down the line with agreeing with Mike Pence, who also recently said that he disagreed with Donald Trump about him being able to overturn the elections and said that he was wrong. Somehow, I am fairly confident. I'm fairly confident on this that Mike Pence will not be on the Trump ticket in 2024. As a matter of fact, there is rumors that Mike Pence is in the works of trying to start a campaign for his own to run in 2024. And to be honest, if if Donald Trump does decide to run, Mike Pence just should not do it. I mean, let's just be honest, it's probably not worth it because it would get ugly. And Mike Pence has said a lot of things that has probably upset a lot of the hardcore Trump supporters, and that will definitely affect his ability to get the nomination in 2024. But we'll see. I mean, it's not even official that Donald Trump is running yet. However, as we all kind of sit back and look at it, it seems kind of pretty official. I mean, the paperwork hasn't been signed. but he clearly is doing some sort of campaigning to a degree. And of course this morning we're off to a good start. We do have an accident that has been reported up on 231 in Youngstown, not terribly bad. So it doesn't look like there's any injuries or the road being blocked up, but it's right over there by 20. So if you're driving in that area, it'll be a little cautious this morning. And then again, like I said, we do have Congressman Dunn coming on this morning. So I do want to do want to get all the questions from you as possible. I've got a list of them myself. He's got some topics that he would like to to talk with us about, but we'll talk with him coming up the seven o'clock hour. We'll have him here for the entire hour, which is always nice. I do like having our local leaders in for more than the 10, 15 minutes that sometimes we're able to get them on the phone. I mean, our local people, it's different. We always get them on for at least 20 minutes, if not more. But I know sometimes when we have a congressperson on or a senator, they're often limited on the time that they've got. So having the congressman in house this morning is going to be once again a nice thing. That last one we did last month We spent a whole hour and it was great. We talked about a lot of different topics. So we'll be looking forward to that coming up at seven o'clock this morning. And of course, if you miss the show or miss the interview, you can one, grab the news talk at 101 app. That way you can take us everywhere you go. Plus, you could also just download the podcast later on this morning or this afternoon or whatever. And you can listen to the interview at that point. So a lot of good things going on up in Canada with the freedom convoy. And of course, the biggest news that hit with the freedom convoy was the GoFundMe account that had about $9 million in it of donations from people around the world who donated to the cause for the freedom convoy. Now $9 million that'd go a long way. Actually today it'll probably go about 50 or 60 miles or so in gas for everybody, but Seriously though, go fund me in their liberal ways. I'm sure you've heard about this story over the weekend, decided that they were going to suspend the account and they were not going to give the money back. Instead, they were going to give the money off to the charities of their choice. Needless to say, that got a lot of people riled up, but the one person that had got riled up, which I think is the reason for why it changed, was Florida Governor Ron DeSantis. When Ron DeSantis jumped in and said, hey, this sounds like some fraud going on here. And I've instructed my attorney general to investigate GoFundMe for fraud. Skirt, also about an hour and a half later, almost two hours later, GoFundMe reversed their decision and decided that they were just going to refund all the donations. Of course, a better idea is to just get out of it, take your cut, and let the donations go. But they, they, they didn't do that, but at least they're returning the money to those who actually donated the money instead of going off and taking the money, which essentially is stealing fraud, taking the money from what was supposed to go to one thing and giving it to whoever they wanted it to go to. So that's a good thing. But the, the freedom cod boy up in Canada is actually going to be heading now to Toronto. And this is going to be fun. I love the fact that Canada is doing this because Canada has been seeing some stuff that just makes you. Oh, it really does. It's very aggravating. I mean, we've seen over the past year, the pastors. who have been arrested in front of their families, in front of their church, all because of the fact that they have defied the government and their lockdowns. As we know now, according to the John Hopkins University, that the lockdowns never worked. So I wonder how the city officials and the province officials are thinking now after doing that to the, and I hope that the pastor sues. I really do. I hope he sues the living daylights out of the government up there in Canada. If they even could do that, I don't know if they can. But, sorry, I just had a, I had an itch in my foot. That is like the worst thing in the world. Had to take my shoe off, put it back on. Multitasking here. But up in Canada, We've seen so many other stupid things going on with the coronavirus quote unquote pandemic happening. And there's a Canadian judge that has now temporarily suspended an unvaccinated father's custody of his three kids, ruling that he poses a health threat to his immune compromised daughter. The court of Queens, bench, judge Natalie Godbot's decision, it was issued, it was last Monday, in which she stated with a heavy heart, she prohibited the father's in-person access to his children, but noted she allowed him generous time to parent his children via phone or video. First off, what kind of crap is that? Well, you know, you could go ahead and parent your children by phone and by video. See, this is the type of stuff that is the reason for why the freedom convoy is going on. The people have had it with government. And really, to be very honest with you, governments in places like Canada, the UK, Australia, here, y'all need to wake up a l