    "turn_text": "But according to the mother's attorney, the children have already received a dose of vaccine. But because of the fact that the father has not received his vaccine. The judge has decided that he's going to take away the custody temporarily of his three children because of the fact that he has a daughter that is immune compromised, who is by the way vaccinated. And more things going on up in Canada, the Ottawa mayor I mean, this is another example of how bad government is around everywhere. And I'm so tired of government officials like this. This is why when you see somebody like this, support their opponent. Straight up, just support their opponent. But the very childless mayor of Ottawa was upset. Mayor Jim Watson described the presence of children playing in bouncy castles at the Freedom Convoy demonstration, and he called it disturbing. Watson, who is a 60 unmarried and without kids. And he said, as he was watching the Ottawa residents living near the demonstration on Parliament Hill and nearby downtown areas, and during a living hell, he claims, and emphasizing that they have been through hell. He also stated that it's disturbing when you see this protest turning into what looks like some kind of a fun carnival. I mean, heaven forbid that we have fun at a protest, right? I mean, what? Are you supposed to peacefully burn buildings down? Is that what you're supposed to be doing? I just want to confirm to see if that's what you're supposed to be doing. But he said that it's disturbing when you see these protests turning into what seems like some kind of fun carnival, where they've got bouncy castles and hot tubs and saunas, a complete insult to the people who are putting up with this nonsense for the last seven days. And it shows great deal of insensitivity. Of course, Breitbart News recorded a video of bouncy castles with playing children on Saturday, and dozens of children were observed with parents attending the demonstrations on and around Wellington Street, which is adjacent to Canada's federal legislature. The CBC, the left wing state funded broadcaster, reported that the presence of saunas and bouncy castles at the protest, which I think is hilarious. I mean, that goes to show you how devoted they are to this. We're so devoted that we're staying hooking up the kids with something to do and some hot tubs and saunas. That is just awesome. I love it. But they said they shouldn't be bringing in hot tubs and they shouldn't be bringing in bouncy castles according to the mayor. This is that is just ridiculous. That should have been stopped. Yeah. You know what people protesting against the government at all or having fun while they're doing it. But I mean, if they needed to stay warm, what should they have done? Better building down, flip a couple of cop cars over, set them on fire. Maybe that would have helped. But the, the CTV news had framed Watson's sexuality as newsworthy back in 2019 and reported it after nearly 40 years the Ottawa mayor has officially come out as gay, which I don't understand what that has to do with the story, but they put it in there anyhow. But Watson wrote a column in the same year titled Mayor Jim Watson after 40 years I'm opening the closet door. Katie Griffin, the CTV anchor, invited Watson to call for military suppression of the protest by the repeating Ottawa police chiefs claim that local police have insufficient resources to fulfill their duties. She claimed that people are losing faith in the city's ability to restore some sort of order. And of course, the whole thing is getting ready to move. Actually, I think it's in the move now in the process. And on top of that, they did close down the city. They shut things down so that more truckers could not actually take part in the big rally. And Ottawa has now actually declared a state of emergency as police are cracking down on the truckers. They've declared the state of emergency as police have begun cracking down on the freedom convoy by cutting off fuel and supply lines. Man, you know, if they did that to those on the left, can you imagine if we shut off fuel and supply to BLM and Antifa? That would have been a mess. But in a press release on Sunday, as the protest over the week over the country's vaccine mandates and coronavirus restrictions headed into its second week, Mayor Jim Watson said that the protesters pose a safety and security threat to the residents of Ottawa. Declaring a state of emergency reflects a serious danger and threat to the safety, security of the residents posed by the ongoing demonstrations and highlights that need for support from other jurisdictions and levels of government. Otherwise put as heaven forbid that you go and protest the government because now all you're doing is getting in the way and you need to be stopped. But I have a bad bad bad word for you guys. It's not going to stop. And now they're moving over to Toronto. They're going to shut down that over there. And of course March 4th is the rumor date for the big freedom convoy here in the US to Washington DC. That's going to make our supply chain suck a little bit more. But you know what? I'm OK with it. Let's do it. Hang on. We got to take a quick break. We'll be right back. This is the Brian Russ Show. You're listening to News Talk at 101. Good morning.",
