    "turn_text": "All right. Welcome back to the show. Thanks so much for listening. So it's the new polls out for our president Biden's approval rating. Still not looking good. Really, really not looking good. As a matter of fact, over half of the country now believes that the United States is on a wrong track over a year into president Biden's presidency. The new rotors router router. How do I always screw that name up? What is it? Reuters. I'm such an idiot. I'm sorry, I really am sometimes. Anyhow, the Reuters IS, what was it? I lost track of where I was here. The IPSOS survey released this week found that the survey, which asked respondents to reveal their current view on the direction of the country, and found that 63% indicated that it is off on the wrong track. 63%. Holy cow. Less than a quarter, 24 percent. I believe the country is headed in the right direction. I think those are the people that are on the Ron Began site. But as a majority of the Republicans and independents, 86 and 67% respectively say that the country is headed down the wrong track. And this comes as a 56% of Americans disapprove of Biden's job performance. And of course, this reflects a six point increase from the 50% who disapproved from last week's poll. And survey also asked respondents to identify what they consider the most important problem facing the U.S. today. and a plurality of them, 25% chose the economy, unemployment, and jobs as the most important problem facing the country today. And that is significant, as President Biden has now vowed to crush the Chinese coronavirus and failed. And he continues to focus on the virus, particularly pushing Americans to continue to wear masks two years into the pandemic, massive, which by the way, John Hopkins University said, yeah, those aren't effective. And neither is the social distancing, neither is the lockdown, but the Biden continues to push it. And what's amazing to me is the sheep that follow it. I still, every time I drive down the road and I see somebody with their mask on while they're in their car by themselves, I just think to myself, oh dear baby Jay, how do you make it through the day? I mean, is it possible for you to be that stupid? But apparently I'm proven wrong every day about what it comes to people being stupid because there's so many of them out there. You just, you shake your head. But on top of, uh, you know, the economy and employment and jobs being an important thing, public health, disease, illness, followed with 12% followed by crime and corruption and the healthcare system along with immigration, uh, were some of the other issues that were that were found in there and per the survey just over one third of independence 34% report to the economy is the most important problem. One quarter 26% of Republican Republicans are also most concerned with the economy while it is still the top issue for Republican. It is a decrease of five points from last week and in contrast, under one in five Democrats think the economy is the most important problem. The biggest problem is Joe Biden. It really, truly is. And now all the vulnerable Democrats that are out there are actually starting to now realize who this isn't good. And Democrats now, especially the vulnerable ones, are starting to really distance themselves a lot from Joe Biden. And that includes people like Senator Ralph Warnock of Georgia, also Mark Kelly of Arizona, neither of which have it called for the president's aid in their campaigns. Remember Warnock, he had President Biden come down during the special election. And Herschel Walker, by the way, is the one that is running up against Raphael Warnock in Georgia. But according to the Washington Post, when Mark Kelly was asked if he wanted Biden to campaign on his behalf, he actually dodged the question. He said, I'm focused on right now on things Arizonians care about, like the price of gasoline and groceries. Mark Kelly also noted that Biden has not been effective on the issue of the Southern border. And Kelly did say that what's going on in the Southern border, at least in Arizona, no, that's not been effective. And Raphael Warnock was equally evasive when asked the question if he wanted the president's help in the campaign. And he said, I know the pundits are focused on the campaign. I am really focused on serving the people of Georgia. And Warnock helped tip the scales a little bit in the U.S. Senate when the Democrats took the favor when he won the Georgia runoff. And he is going to most likely be running against Herschel Walker in the upcoming election in November. But there's a few others too. Senator Kathleen Cortez Masto of Nevada said that the president is always welcome in my state, but she hesitated to call herself a Biden Democrat. other Democrats hope that Biden's fundraising efforts and his overall personality will help them, help them, you know, come in ahead in the midterms. Representative Dan Bayer of Virginia believes that the president's approval rating will increase as the economy gets better. But the economy's not getting better, buddy. I don't know if you haven't noticed that. Yeah, but that employment is like skyrocketing, which I love. I love this argument. when uh... when we hear from circle back saki and in the white house about how unen the unemployment numbers are so fantastic which essentially all they did is they took water from one bucket put into the other and said look buckets fall which by the way the water that was in the other bucket came from the bucket that they just filled and over the course of uh... the spring and summer Uh, one of the Democrats of the, uh, the bear, Dan bear said that we'd love to see president Biden at 47 or 49 or 50%. And now we'll make all the difference in those elections. I don't think it's going to make a difference in the election. And this is the thing that kills me sometimes about politicians is that they look too much at numbers and not reality. You know, the thing is people have suffered under Joe Biden's presidency for the past year. We watch on a continuous basis as he does what he does. People are losing faith and confidence in President Biden in just incredible droves. There are more Democrats now that are regretting their decision to vote for him. And he's done nothing. I mean, there is nothing that Joe Biden has done that makes a Democrat want to actually jump on that and say, look what we did, Mom. Because the reality is you haven't done anything. Haven't done anything good at all. But we got the infrastructure deal. Yeah, the infrastructure deal that nobody likes. But we're working on getting build back better. We'll get it. No, you're not going to get it. Because the American people have spoken and said, no, knock it off. But we're working on voting rights. What are you talking about? We already have the voting rights. It's there. It's the law. What are you talking about? Well, we're going to stop the Republicans and all those big bad evil plans they've got. You mean the ones that are actually designed to make it so that my vote counts in a campaign stolen by somebody dropping off a box of ballots? Come on. I mean, some politicians, I swear to God, they are so blind and so tucked into their bubble that they don't get it. They don't get it at all with reality around them. And it really does make me laugh to see that. And I honestly don't think that there is much that Joe Biden is going to be able to this year to turn around his favorability. When you've got 63% of the country saying that we are on the wrong track, look, you know, primaries are coming up in what August? So you got February, March, April, May, June, July, like seven months, seven months to go. You got to have to do a lot of improvement to change people's minds in seven months. Not to mention, you think about all the things that have gone wrong during this one year. I don't see President Biden's approval rating making that much of a reverse course that's going to help some of these vulnerable Democrats. I mean, we're already at what 28 Democrats that have already saw the T leaves and went, you know, we're out. Even Nancy Pelosi's people saw the T leaves and they're like, no, we're out of here gone. See you later. Bye. Gotta go. Even though Nancy Pelosi doesn't see it and she's like, I'm going to run again. Oh, where's the bar? It's gonna be a disastrous year. 2022 is gonna be a disastrous year for Democrats. And I love the ones that don't see it. The ones who think everything's gonna be okay because, you know, Joe Biden, you know, he's got that great personality and everybody loves Joe. I mean, look, he's eating ice cream. How relatable is that? It's just not gonna work for you guys. It really isn't. I mean, if the Democrat Party really, truly wants to get smart about things, they need to look at what has failed. and correct the actions, correct the ideology. Just look at it and see it. It doesn't take much to realize what has failed. But they don't see it. They don't see it at all. Anyhow, coming up seven o'clock hour, we have Congressman Neil Dunn is going to be joining us on the show. Also, later on this week, we have, did I say Senator Congressman? Congressman Neil Dunn, Senator Marco Rubio is going to be joining us on the show later on this week too. Of course, still looking for your questions for Congressman Dunn, hit me up on our Facebook page or the website. Hang on, we'll be right back.",
