f the most dangerous people for this country. I mean, he's wanted dead or alive in some countries around the world. I mean, when that's the case, you know that you got a guy that's a problem. And yet he's able to not only walk around, but he's able to throw millions and millions of dollars into our political campaigns and look at the problems that he has caused. So again, I just don't get it why this guy has allowed to do this. I don't understand why he's not in cuffs. And that and, you know, for all these countries that have these warrants out for him, why are we still covering him? I mean, if that was you or I, I mean, hey, look, Julian Assange, I mean, he came out and he just leaked some information that, oh sure, maybe he shouldn't have, but when you stop looking at the information, kind of glad that he did. And you look at everything that went on with him, Why do we cover for George Soros? I don't get it. But Stacey Abrams, her campaign got into a little bit of trouble over the weekend with a maskless photo surrounded by masked children. And remember, Stacey, she trusts the science. Her campaign had responded on Sunday to a massive uproar over Stacey Abrams' viral maskless photo and accusing critics in the photo of using a black history month reading event to attack Stacey Abrams and claiming Abrams trust science. The campaign manager for Stacey Abrams gubernatorial race first responded to the black backlash on Sunday afternoon by taking swipes at Georgia's Democrats top two potential opponents along with incumbent Governor Brian Kemp and former Senator David Perdue as both chastised Abrams for displaying hypocrisy in a photo. And in our campaign manager wrote on social media, our opponents take a brief break from licking Trump's boots this weekend to issue baseless attacks and then claimed that our opponents are using a Black History Month reading event for Georgia children as the infamous for a false political attack. And of course, this was the photo that was taken with Stacey Abrams there without a mask with all these kids. I just love the hypocrisy. It's okay. She held her breath though, so it's all right. That's just like the mayor of LA. and the governor of California, when they got busted at the LA Lakers, not the LA Rams game for not having their mask on when they were taking pictures with Magic Johnson. The response they said was, at least the mayor said this, I held my breath during the photo.",
