hool without permission. And earlier in the week, a video containing reported audio from an assistant principal of Loudon County Elementary School was posted to social media and then went viral. Totally, these idiots in Loudon County, they just can't get it straight at all. I mean, if it wasn't so serious, it would almost be funny. But in the video, the assistant principal can be heard warning parents that their children who violate protocols will be held in school restriction situation until they are picked up and will be considered trespassing if they return to the campus. And he said, until you arrive, your children will be held in an in school restriction situation here at the school. It is important that I point out to you stated in the letter that you will that you'll receive that they are not allowed on campus or on Loudoun County Public School property starting tomorrow. It will be considered trespassing. She added a spokesperson for Loudoun County also had told W USA nine that trespassing charges are not common. Ziegler added that no students have been arrested as a result of returning to school while under suspension. But the Loudoun County Public School System does have the authority to arrest or charge any suspended students or their parents for trespassing. Furthermore, LCPS has not requested that local law enforcement charge any student with trespassing in connection to recent suspensions. And the spokesperson for the Loudoun County ended up telling the TV station that students who do not wear masks may be suspended for up to 10 days. And that suspension would be for willful or continued disobedience of school rules. Guys, they've already proven your school rules to be, well, ineffective in not working and wrong. But here we go, Loudon County, they just, they're digging themselves so deep and they continue going after the parents too and I just love it. But Ziggler continued on saying that I want to emphasize that despite some unverified reports in the